														Group vs. group tactics: player group vs. player group.<br />
<br />
Most of us dont' have a lot of experience in this, where we fight players, who are far more unpredictable and flexible than ANY mobs we have ever encountered.  <br />
<br />
Think about it! What's our usual tactic? Tanks around the mob to absorb aggro and damage, everybody dots or nukes and the thing dies.  Ad infinitum, ad nauseum.<br />
<br />
Now, imagine group vs. group.  The tanks go into melee, now that's gonna take a while, 'cause the casters will be very busy.  The enchanters try to mez some of the casters, maybe one of the enemy tanks, and have them attack their friends.  Chain stuns go to other casters, especially the healers.  Root and dot the tanks, they're stuck with each other until the root wears off.<br />
AOE nukes might come into play, but mana and hitpoints are draining rapidly. <br />
<br />
Keep in mind that, during all this, you're not fighting one mob at a time, you're fighting six mobs.<br />
<br />
This is really a much different style of fighting or playing than most of us are used to.  And if you haven't played PvP--and I haven't, but I'm considering it just to learn how--it can be a different experience than you've ever had.<br />
<br />
Meeting in the Arena to learn this stuff should be particularly instructive.  <br />
<br />
Just some random thoughts and my two coppers worth.<br />
<br />
Ollie						</td>
